      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Foundry/CodeInterpreterBridge.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/Middleware/AgentServiceRoutingMiddleware.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SprkChatAgentFactory.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/AgentServiceNodeExecutor.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/LegalResearchHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Foundry/AgentServiceOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="read">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Cache/TenantCache.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>The cache id MUST NOT be a compile-time constant on any path that caches.</constraint>
    <constraint>No caller may pass a literal where the tenant argument belongs.</constraint>
    <constraint>Do NOT modify AgentConfigurationService or ModuleEntitlementResolver — verified non-violations; changing them causes harm.</constraint>
    <constraint>Do NOT attempt customer separation in the key. That is the dedicated Redis instance (ADR-009 amended) and task 123.</constraint>
    <constraint>CodeInterpreterBridge must create a fresh thread per call rather than resume — match its own stated contract.</constraint>
    <constraint>A missing conversation id must FAIL, not fall back to a shared default (ADR-003). A silent fallback reinstates the defect.</constraint>
    <constraint>Update the XML docs and AgentServiceOptions comments that state the old `agent-thread:{tenantId}` key pattern — a comment describing a retired key shape is how this survived review.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-009-redis-caching.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-lean-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/D-12-deployment-model-redefinition.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Re-verify every line reference above, and run the affected suites green BEFORE editing.</step>
    <step>Change `CreateOrResumeThreadAsync` (and `InvalidateThreadCacheAsync`) to require an explicit conversation scope; make the cache id carry it.</step>
    <step>Thread `sessionId` from `SprkChatAgentFactory` into `AgentServiceRoutingMiddleware`.</step>
    <step>Point the playbook node at `context.RunId` and legal research at `context.ChatSessionId`.</step>
    <step>Make `CodeInterpreterBridge` create a fresh thread per call, and delete the synthetic tenant key.</step>
    <step>Add a negative control: two different conversation scopes MUST produce different cache keys, and a constant/empty scope MUST be rejected.</step>
    <step>Prove it by seeding — revert one caller to a constant and confirm a test fails.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A caller is found with no conversation-scope identifier in reach — do NOT invent one or reuse tenantId; escalate, because a fabricated scope silently reinstates sharing.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any additional `CreateOrResumeThreadAsync` caller beyond the four enumerated — the inventory was incomplete.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>`CreateOrResumeThreadAsync` cannot be called without a conversation scope, enforced by the signature.</criterion>
    <criterion>Zero compile-time-constant cache ids remain on the agent-thread path.</criterion>
    <criterion>Two distinct sessions produce two distinct cache keys — asserted, not assumed.</criterion>
    <criterion>An empty or whitespace conversation scope is rejected rather than defaulted.</criterion>
    <criterion>`CodeInterpreterBridge` performs no cache read or write.</criterion>
    <criterion>`LegalResearchHandler` passes no literal into the tenant argument.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every XML doc / options comment stating `agent-thread:{tenantId}` is corrected.</criterion>
    <criterion>`AgentConfigurationService` and `ModuleEntitlementResolver` are UNCHANGED.</criterion>
    <criterion>Full Spaarke.ArchTests green; BFF unit suite green; `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Authored 2026-09-29 (session 25). Corrects the item-6 scope: 1 of the 3 listed sites is a real violation, and the list missed the two constant-tenant callers, which are worse. Sibling task 123 covers the customer discriminator (D-14).</notes>
</task>
